# UniVRMXT repository

- Package id: `com.vrmxt.univrmxt`. Target Unity floor from `package.json`
  (`2022.3`); do not silently raise Unity, package, API compatibility, or C# language
  requirements.
- Keep first-party code in this package tree (`Runtime`, `Editor`, `Tests`, `Samples~`
  as used nearby). Do not nest a full player app or Warudo plugin inside the UPM package.
- Select namespace and dependencies from nearby code and the nearest `.asmdef`.
- Runtime assemblies must not reference Editor assemblies or `UnityEditor`.
  Put editor-only code under an `Editor` folder and editor-only asmdef.
- When crossing an assembly boundary, update the owning `.asmdef` deliberately.
  Avoid adding broad or circular references.
- Preserve VRM 1.0 load without UniVRMXT and optional `VRMXT_*` attach/export behavior.
  Avoid unrelated cleanup that widens the public API.
- Stock UniVRM / UniGLTF live in consuming projects or as package dependencies — edit
  those sources only in their owning repos (e.g. Extended-UniVRM), not by forking copies
  into this package.
